  "label": "White man in prayer is mapped as the 'how black people became christians' narrative",
  "description": "The visual of the white man praying with a rosary is analogically mapped to the text 'how black people became christians'. This mapping implies that the white man represents the 'proper' or 'authentic' form of Christian practice, while the text suggests that Black people were somehow 'converted' or 'forced' into Christianity, reinforcing a racialized hierarchy. The man's posture and the rosary symbolize a white, Catholic, and passive form of Christianity, which is contrasted with the implied active, self-determined Black Christian identity that the text dismisses. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it dehumanizes Black religious identity by portraying it as something imposed rather than self-chosen.",
